[Term]
id: PAIN:0000053
name: acute pain
def: "Pain of recent onset and probable limited duration, usually having an identifiable temporal and causal relationship to injury or disease." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.iasp-pain.org/resources/topics/acute-pain/"}
comment: Acute pain is caused by injury, surgery, illness, trauma, or painful medical procedures and generally lasts from a few minutes to less than six months. Acute pain usually disappears whenever the underlying cause is treated or healed.
is_a: PAIN:0000128 ! temporally specified pain
