[Term]
id: PAIN:0000092
name: chronic widespread pain
def: "Chronic pain that is diffuse and experienced in body regions and in at least 3 or more body quadrants (as defined by upper-lower/left-right side of the body) and axial skeleton (neck, back, chest, and abdomen)." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.findacode.com/icd-11/code-849253504.html", IAO:0000119="PMID:39445928"}
comment: Chronic widespread pain (CWP) is associated with significant emotional distress (anxiety, anger/frustration or depressed mood) or functional disability (interference in daily life activities and reduced participation in social roles). CWP is multifactorial: biological, psychological and social factors contribute to the pain syndrome. The diagnosis is appropriate when the pain is not directly attributable to a nociceptive process in these regions and there are features consistent with nociplastic pain and identified psychological and social contributors. {terms:source="https://www.findacode.com/icd-11/code-849253504.html"}
intersection_of: PAIN:0000040 ! chronic pain
intersection_of: RO:0000053 PATO:0001566 ! has characteristic distributed
property_value: IAO:0000589 "chronic widespread pain (PAIN)" xsd:string
property_value: skos:note "Additional criteria to consider:\n- Include quantrants/regions of body in the definition. \n  - E.g., >= 3 quadrants & axial\n  - >= 4 body regions\n- Use the notion of functional region instead of regions divided by joints.\n\ndefine as chronic & multi-localized." xsd:string
