[Term]
id: PAIN:0000104
name: dysesthesia
def: "An unpleasant abnormal sensory experience, whether spontaneous or evoked." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.iasp-pain.org/resources/terminology"}
is_a: EMRO:0000005 ! sensory experience
property_value: IAO:0000589 "dysesthesia (PAIN)" xsd:string
property_value: skos:closeMatch "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C28246" xsd:string
property_value: skos:closeMatch "http://snomed.info/id/279079003" xsd:string
property_value: skos:relatedMatch "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0012534" xsd:string
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9625-1899
property_value: terms:created "2026-07-01T17:55:31Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:description "An unpleasant abnormal sensation, whether spontaneous or evoked. Note: Compare with pain and with paresthesia. Special cases of dysesthesia include hyperalgesia and allodynia. A dysesthesia should always be unpleasant and a paresthesia should not be unpleasant, although it is recognized that the borderline may present some difficulties when it comes to deciding as to whether a sensation is pleasant or unpleasant. It should always be specified whether the sensations are spontaneous or evoked.\nSee entry in https://www.iasp-pain.org/resources/terminology." xsd:string

