id: PAIN:0010272
name: neurovascular orofacial pain
def: "Attacks of variable duration of moderate or severe intraoral pain, without head pain, often accompanied by toothache-like symptoms, with mild autonomic and/or migrainous symptoms. Two subforms are represented by patients with relatively short attacks (1–4 hours) and those with longer attacks (>4 hours)." []
comment: ICOP number: 5.4
subset: PAIN:0010296
is_a: PAIN:0010255 ! orofacial pain with headache presentation
property_value: IAO:0000119 "PMID:32103673" xsd:string
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5583-4731
property_value: terms:created "2025-07-07T17:28:50Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: PAIN:0010273
name: short-lasting neurovascular orofacial pain
def: "Neurovascular orofacial pain that lasts between 1-4 hours." []
comment: ICOP number: 5.4.1
