[Term]
id: UBERON:0002470
name: autopod region
def: "Terminal segment of free limb, immediately distal to the zeugopod region. The fully developed autopod consists of the autopod skeleton plus associated structures such as integument, muscle tissue, vasculature etc. The autopod is divided into mesopodial, metapodiual, and acropodial segments. Examples: human hand, mouse paw, human foot." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/303, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
